          "id": "4046277",
          "title": "Discovery Session Demo",
          "duration": "4:34",
          "durationMinutes": 5,
          "description": "Okay. So throughout the course, we're gonna make reference to\nDiscovery Session Demo\n\nDemo video walking through a discovery session.\n\nEssential Questions Demo Document for a CPA Company \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTranscript\n\n﻿Okay, so throughout the course,\n\nwe're going to make reference to\n\nthe essential questions document.\n\nThis is going to be our guide that\n\nwe, you know, we do our strategy\n\nsession, but then we're going to\n\ncome back to this whenever we\n\nstart writing copy for our website.\n\nAnd so we have a bunch of examples\n\nthat we show here.\n\nYou know, as far as who is the\n\nprimary target audience.\n\nWe started to talk through a solar\n\npanel company, business\n\nconsultant, weight loss coach.\n\nWe have some examples written in here.\n\nAnd we're going to write copy and\n\ncreate a website for a solar panel\n\ninstaller, solar panel company.\n\nBut also we're going to write copy\n\nfor an accountant.\n\nSo a CPA client.\n\nAnd so I'm going to walk through\n\nthis document because we're going\n\nto make reference to this as we go\n\nthroughout the course.\n\nAnd this is really kind of going\n\nto demo the types of answers that\n\nwe're looking for when we're\n\ninterviewing a client.\n\nSo this first one, who is the\n\nprimary target audience?\n\nAnd so we're working with the CPA\n\ncompany, and this may be something\n\nthat they would be saying.\n\nSo primarily small business\n\nowners, age 30 to 55, could be\n\nmale or female, college age,\n\ngraduate or above.\n\nAnd so when you talk to your\n\nclient and they start doing, you\n\nknow, giving you all kinds of\n\nanswers, you want to really kind\n\nof summarize and condense because\n\nyou're going to have all kinds of\n\nnotes and you want to pull out the\n\nmain points and really condense it.\n\nAnd so here's some of the main points.\n\nWhat is it that that person wants\n\nand what are they trying to achieve?\n\nAnd so this is really just high level.\n\nYou may get a whole lot of notes,\n\nbut after you get all the notes,\n\nyou want to try and condense it\n\ndown to the most essential things.\n\nThey want\n\na CPA who can help their business\n\nrun more smoothly with\n\nbookkeeping, accounting and taxes.\n\nSo we're really trying to get the\n\nhigh level messages.\n\nBiggest problems your ideal client\n\nis facing as it relates to what\n\nyou sell.\n\nThey don't have time, don't have\n\ncapacity, don't have know how.\n\nAnd so we're pulling out the main\n\nmessages for this\n\nCPA client.\n\nWhat are the trigger moments that\n\ncause this person to realize they\n\nhave a problem?\n\nSo they're feeling overwhelmed and\n\nstressed about tax time.\n\nSo a lot of times we're trying to\n\nfigure out, like, what is the\n\nthing that caused them to reach\n\nout there?\n\nTheir monthly financial review\n\nisn't getting done.\n\nSo what are those trigger moments?\n\nWhat are the top emotions their\n\nproblems are causing?\n\nAnxious about not getting it right.\n\nUncertain.\n\nSee, these are all emotions.\n\nUncertain, overwhelmed, confused.\n\nSo we want to really pull out\n\nthose messages during this section.\n\nHow are these problems affecting\n\nthem financially?\n\nSo it might be paying too much in\n\ntaxes or too little and worried\n\nabout having to pay penalties.\n\nThis takes too much time and is\n\nkeeping the business owner away\n\nfrom doing more profitable things.\n\nSo, again, as you interview your\n\nclient, they may see a whole lot\n\nof other things, but you want to\n\nget the high level messaging down.\n\nWhat unpleasant event or\n\noccurrence are they trying to avoid?\n\nHaving to pay penalties to the government.\n\nBeing seen as unorganized.\n\nWhat have they tried in the past\n\nto solve their problem?\n\nTried to do it on their own.\n\nDown here, what wasn't working\n\nabout these past solutions?\n\nWhat are the reasons why they want\n\na new solution?\n\nSo DIY, bookkeeping and accounting\n\nis stressful.\n\nAlways worried about doing\n\nsomething wrong.\n\nThis next one, why is it wrong for\n\nyour customers to be experiencing\n\nall these problems?\n\nWhat do you believe they deserve instead?\n\nEvery business owner deserves\n\nfinancial guidance that supports\n\ntheir growth.\n\nAnd so as we start going through\n\nthis document, you're going to see\n\nexamples the whole way through for\n\nour CPA client.\n\nAnd the big thing is when you\n\ninterview someone, you're going to\n\nget a lot of notes.\n\nWhat you want to do is go back\n\nthrough and really condense them\n\ndown to the high level messaging\n\nbecause they're going to say all\n\nkinds of stuff.\n\nAnd you want to just pull out the\n\nsimplest messages and\n\nput this\n\ninto this document.\n\nAnd it's going to be easier for\n\nyou to make reference to later on\n\nwhen you start writing the website copy.\n\nSo you walk through all these\n\nthings with your client.\n\nThis is basically an example of a\n\nCPA client and the answers that\n\nthey might give for a website and\n\nstrategy project.\n\nSo this is a basically strategy\n\nsession and all the answers for a\n\nCPA client.\n\nNow, keep reference to this\n\ndocument because this document,\n\nwe're going to come back to it\n\nas we start wireframing and\n\nwriting copy for our website, for\n\nour CPA client.",
