          "id": "4047082",
          "title": "AI Writing Prompts",
          "duration": "10:00",
          "durationMinutes": 10,
          "description": "Useful AI Website Copywriting Prompts:\nRESEARCH PROMPTS:\n\n\n*Reference the Essential Questions Doc \n\nMy business is {industry} and provides {service}. Who would be our primary audience?\n\n\n\n\nWhen it comes to my service, what are my customers trying to achieve?\n\n\n\n\nWhat are the biggest problems my customer is facing that makes them need the service I provide?\n\n\n\n\nWhen does my customer first realize they need a service like mine?\n\n\n\n\nWhat are the top emotions my customer's problems are causing? \n\n\n\n\nHow do these problems affect them financially?\n\n\n\n\nWhat unpleasant event or occurrence are my customers trying to avoid?\n\n\n\n\nWhat have my customers tried in the past to solve their problems?\n\n\n\n\nWhat wasn’t working about these past solutions? What are the reasons why they want a new solution?\n\n\n\n\nWhat do my customers deserve instead of having to deal with these problems?\n\n\n\n\nDescribe how my service solves my customer's problems. \n\n\n\n\nWhat are the biggest tangible benefits to using our solution? \n\n\n\n\nWhat are the biggest emotional benefits to using our solution?\n\n\n\n\nWhat does my ideal client want more than anything else? If they waved a magic wand, what would the best outcome be?\n\n\n\n\nHow would my audience explain the “reasons why” the price of my offer is an absolute no-brainer investment for them?\n\n\n\n\nWhat is the cost of not buying my offer? How bad can things become if they don’t buy?\n\n\n\n\nWhat are ways we can differentiate our offer from other companies like ours?\n\n\n\n\nAre there any promises or guarantees we could make with our product or service?\n\n\n\n\nWhat are the most common objections someone has to buying our product or service?\n\n\n\n\nHow could we overcome these objections?\n\n\n\n\nWhat does a simple 3-4 step process look like for someone purchasing our product or service?\n\n\n\n\nBrainstorm what sections I might want on my homepage, about page, services page, etc. \n\n\nWRITING PROMPTS:\nHeadlines\n\n\nNote: Many headlines AI gives you are more for ad copy vs. website copy. They are often overly gimmick and more about the click. For website copywriting, we recommend simple and clear copy vs. ad copy. That’s why the prompts below are simplistic in structure.\n\nI am a {insert industry} company providing {insert service/solution}. Write me a list of headline ideas using the… \n\n{Outcome} + {Solution} framework \n\n{Solution} + {Outcome} framework\n\n{Solution} without {Pain} framework\n\n{Solution} in {time-frame} framework\n\n{Solution} without {Pain} in {time-frame} framework\n\n{Solution} with {Success} in {time-frame} framework\n\nSubheadlines\n\nMy headline is {insert headline}. Write a subheadline that describes what I provide in slightly more detail using the … \n\n{Outcome} + {Solution} framework \n\n{Solution} + {Outcome} framework\n\n{Solution} without {Pain} framework\n\n{Strong Verb} {Outcome} with {Benefit} framework\n\nDescriptions\n\nMy product/service is {insert description}. Write a short paragraph description using the {Problem}, {Solution}, {Outcome} framework \n\n\nREWRITING/EDITING PROMPTS: \n\nHow could I make this {insert content} stronger?\n\n\n\n\nSummarize or simplify {insert content}\n\n\n\n\nTurn {insert content} into bullet points\n\n\n\n\nRewrite, eliminating filler words\n\n\n\n\nRewrite these feature descriptions into benefits for the end user\n\n\n\n\nRewrite this using power words\n\n\n\n\nRewrite/adapt to US / UK / AU / CA English \n\n\n\n\nRewrite to a 5th-grade level\n\n\n\n\nRewrite using {tone of voice}\n\nProfessional\n\nFriendly \n\nHumorous \n\nWhitty\n\nInspirational\n\nCasual\n\nIntellectual\n\nStorytelling\n\nMinimalist\n\nPersuasive \n\nAdventurous\n\n\n\n\nReformat this {insert lengthy text} into an easy-to-scan version with bullet points and headings\n\n\n\n\n\nImprove/fix {insert content} grammar\n\n\n\n\n\nAdd relevant emojis for each bullet",
